from pathlib import Path
import json
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;root=Path.cwd();unit=root/'docs/plans/definition-formal-assurance/candidate/assurance-snapshots-v1/definitions/cal.definition.coordination-context';report=json.loads((unit/'carrier-consumer-inspection.json').read_bytes());assert report['check_count']==288 and len(report['unresolved_consumer_findings'])==15
text='''# Coordination Context consumer correspondence review

The current inspection passes 288 exact-source, carrier, projection, catalog and finite comparison checks. It accounts for twenty-five proposed source coordinates, fifty-six schema probes, eleven Definition schema probes and thirty fresh hypothetical T/I comparisons. These observations are bounded by the exact selected bytes and the extracted pure functions. They neither decode a real carrier into an accepted interpretation nor accept a source-to-consumer map. All fifteen consumer findings and twenty-one source-owner findings remain unresolved.

The current artifact-type registry contains 143 contracts and 121 current identities. Every current artifact and schema selected by the registry was checked against its exact digest. Coordination Context/v2 is the one current complete direct binding to this exact Definition; v1 has the same Definition binding but its effective state is historical. Both immutable package bodies and their fixtures retain candidate-unadmitted labels and authority_effect none. Those historical labels are preserved alongside positive admission overlays. A type admission can change effective type state without rewriting its body or admitting every example instance. The distinction is part of the evidence, rather than an inconsistency to hide.

C21 admits seven CTX01 Artifact Types and creates zero operational context-owner bindings or context instances. C67 admits the exact Coordination Context/v2 successor, transitions one predecessor to historical and creates zero instances, consumer activations or relation endpoint pairs. C70 has a different scope: its one ordinary instance admission is the exact integrated Governed Model. It excludes other ordinary Artifact Type instances, Typed Relations and runtime or consumer activations. These decision scopes cannot be combined to claim that a Coordination Context fixture or the Ontology Product record is operationally admitted. The semantic admission of the Definition under C18 also supplies no accepted formal translation.

The v1 schema wrapper points to a local coordinationContext definition inside the shared CTX01 schema. Inspection constructs that exact local validation schema in memory, preserves the wrapper and binds both files. This avoids fetching a remote schema or executing a package writer. The shared generator's literal configuration and pure rendering functions are extracted from its AST. The v2 schema is directly closed and its pure renderer, semantic-failure function, lifecycle comparison and relation projection are separately extracted. Both versions reproduce their exact existing artifact and positive-witness Markdown projections twice without mutating the input. Canonical source direction remains machine record to generated view.

Product is one nonempty scalar reference in both schemas. Missing and multiple-Product probes reject shape. Project and Goal each admit null or one nonempty scalar reference. Their presence is independent. V1 permits an optional field to be omitted; v2 makes the field mandatory and uses explicit null to represent absence. The four positive v2 fixtures demonstrate Product only, Product with Project, Product with Goal and Product with both. The typed candidate separately represents presence flags and nominated references. Its total function tables do not force an absent anchor to acquire a meaning. An accepted map must state how absent fields, null values, presence predicates and selected reference bindings correspond.

Neither a scalar Product nor an optional reference resolves an actual Product, Project or Goal revision. Those identities require source-qualified evidence and accepted relationships to their own definitions. Printed reference strings are not merged with the independently qualified sorted carriers. The schemas reject empty anchor strings and arrays of multiple anchors, but passing those restrictions does not prove reference resolution, correct scope or owner authority. The carrier's chosen representation can be a sensible implementation while remaining an unaccepted denotation hypothesis for this theory.

Bounded Context references may be empty in both carriers. When present, lists nominate explicit references and reject unsupported embedded semantic-boundary fields through their closed schemas. The v1 semantic subset checks that domain_model_ref, ubiquitous_language_ref and context_map_refs do not appear in the coordination record. V2 adds comparisons between the coordination identity, Product, Project, Goal and boundary-reference strings, as well as owner and endpoint strings. These checks observe raw identifier separation. They do not authenticate distinct meanings or prove that a boundary is independently owned. The source theory requires a separately declared independence relationship, and does not force different principal identifiers for independent ownership roles.

The Ontology Product coordination record supplies an actual current v1 candidate surface for inspection. It passes the historical v1 shape and reproduces its exact generated Markdown. It explicitly nominates cal.context.governance/v2 and cal.context.ontology-lifecycle/v2. Available boundary files live in v3 directories but declare 2.0.0-candidate.1 versions. They use semantic_owner_ref rather than the coordination record's owner_ref. The observation records the actual selector, exact file bytes, identity and version separately. Directory version labels, nominated /v2 strings and declared semantic versions are not silently treated as an accepted resolution rule. The semantic owner nominations are not operational principal bindings.

Lifecycle has a different representation across versions. V1 exposes a lifecycle posture through classification. V2 has a lifecycle_state, owner_route and predecessor_ref, alongside its classification posture. A proposed lifecycle map must distinguish these coordinates. Neither an active state nor an empty revision_history proves durable storage or an authentic history. Owner, owner route and challenge route strings nominate relationships; they do not identify a live accountable principal or execute a challenge process. No current service, agent, owner handler or runtime is invoked by this review.

The v2 lifecycle function compares Product, Project, Goal and purpose values between base and after records. Any change with the same identity returns successor-required. A changed identity with the correct predecessor string returns successor-identity-present; without that link it returns successor-link-missing. When no anchors differ, a same identity and nonempty revision history returns same-identity-revision-permitted. This function has no materiality input. It therefore represents a policy stronger than the candidate's necessary source condition if it is applied to every anchor difference. The Definition leaves the meaning of material change to an accepted interpretation. Current carrier behavior cannot silently become that interpretation.

The source-qualified candidate distinguishes the original context, independently nominated desired anchors, a materiality flag and the successor context. Its material-change guard requires an anchor difference, distinct successor identity, a successor relation and matching desired anchors, including optional presence. Four negative controls independently reject in-place material Product, Project, Goal and purpose changes. Removing the respective materiality flags leaves T true while losing the required material-change coverage populations. This is evidence for the selected finite formulas and for the separation of T from I, not a policy decision about which real changes are material.

The current lifecycle fixture matrix is replayed with the extracted function and its explicit expected outcomes. Shape validation alone permits a record copy with changed Product and the same identity; the isolated lifecycle function requires succession for that pair. These are different checks over different input scopes. A before/after pair, an authenticated change record and a single closed schema instance are not interchangeable. The candidate preserves before and desired state separately to catch circular succession tests. Neither a predecessor string nor a returned success label creates a successor or validates a real lineage.

Source-view change has a separate type in the candidate and preserves the nominated coordination identity. These carriers do not expose direct before/after source-view snapshot coordinates. A source-policy revision fixture demonstrates one same-identity revision behavior, but it is not a complete source-view correspondence. The current proposed matrix leaves view references as explicit unresolved coordinates. A future accepted map must identify the actual information view, policy relationship, immutable before/after evidence and the classification that separates view-only changes from material anchor changes. Equal identities and policy arrays cannot establish those relationships by themselves.

The v2 relation projection function emits relation.frames for Product, optional Project and Goal, and each Bounded Context reference. If a predecessor is present it also emits successor-of. The inspection checks the exact relation count and that extraction does not mutate the original fixture. These are pure data projections from nominated fields. C67 excludes relation endpoint admission and Typed Relation creation. Relation endpoint-extension residue remains in the package. A projection does not acquire semantic authority merely because its label matches a Relation Kind elsewhere in the repository. An accepted map needs exact endpoints, qualifiers and authority scope.

Closed schema probes reject injected accepted_semantic_map_ref, execution_permission_ref and embedded semantic-boundary fields. They also reject empty identity, owner, purpose and challenge strings. Both schemas impose minimum one for consumers and intended uses. That is a carrier policy; the Definition does not state a universal cardinality minimum for those collections. The theory therefore keeps nominated collection carriers separate from their actual membership and suitability. Empty boundary references remain permitted. Boundary identity, ownership, adequacy of source policies and completeness of a consumer list remain further obligations even when shape is accepted.

Definition schema probes make a separate point about authority. Removing required structural fields rejects shape. Replacing normative text with other well-formed text can still pass the schema. Schema correctness does not determine whether the new text preserves the admitted meaning. The candidate avoids modifying the Definition and instead binds exact source bytes, spans, formula selections and unresolved losses. Current positive admission and pure projection parity are necessary evidence about selected artifacts, but neither substitutes for source-owner fidelity review. The proposed formal sorts remain candidate vocabulary rather than new canonical definitions.

Thirty fresh hypothetical models compare selected T clauses and required I populations independently. They exercise exact bindings, cardinality, boundary membership, independent ownership, identity preservation, matched successors, materiality and legitimately absent optional references. The models are explicit supplied interpretations; they are not claimed to be decoded from a fixture through an accepted denotation map. Their digests, complete models, clause results, population results and evaluator step counts are recorded. Passing supplied finite models establishes those calculations. It does not establish a joint whole-definition interpretation, actual populations, all possible contexts or consistent shared meanings across dependencies.

Three consumer-checker failures are retained before correction. The discovery rows contained byte counts in addition to the path and digest fields expected by the existing exact-reference checker. The discovery acceptance field was named accepted_consumer_maps. The boundary records used semantic_owner_ref. Each correction reads the actual data shape and preserves exact prior bytes and diagnostics. No carrier, source Definition, formula, control expectation or verifier limit was changed to force success. These retained failures are part of the final delivery evidence and remain distinct from successful source-owner or consumer acceptance, which has not occurred.

The pending coordinate map covers all twenty-five non-handle functions in the primary theory. A selected carrier field can have a proposed interpretation, several different meanings can share a printed field, and a source coordinate can have no selected direct field. Each outcome is recorded explicitly. Owner references, lifecycle, purpose stability, history, source-view snapshots, materiality, semantic-boundary version resolution, actual permission and source fidelity still require accepted denotations. Proposals and explicit residue account for the questions; they do not answer them with authority.

The next completion gates are qualified authority profiles, static reuse validation, reachable dependencies, whole111 inventory, six fresh full-delivery checks, full aspect review, seal and a separate audit. The existing seventeen typed inputs and five checker bindings remain frozen. The original episode still requires 183 identities, 189 versions, 201 source files, 121 tasks, 511 planning edges, 797 work units, 36 frontiers, T/O/E/R/J and the final complete explanation. An explicitly unresolved outcome can satisfy only an original acceptance alternative that permits it. It does not waive an artifact or convert the episode into a count of partial theories.

Unresolved consumer findings:

'''
text+='\n'.join('- '+row['finding_id']+': '+row['issue'] for row in report['unresolved_consumer_findings'])+'\n'
